# Commits that moved text without changing code.
#
# `git blame` credits a line to whatever commit last touched it, so a
# repo-wide reformat makes every reflowed line look like it was written
# on the day of the reformat. Listing that commit here tells blame to
# walk past it to the commit that actually changed the code.
#
# This file is only half of it. Blame reads it locally only if the clone
# is configured to:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# GitHub's web blame reads it without any configuration.
#
# Add only commits that provably changed no code, and only after they are
# pushed — a rebased or amended SHA listed here makes blame fail.
# Full 40-character SHAs; short ones are rejected.

# Let the formatter have the files it had been losing to
# `dart format` across 22 files; whitespace and trailing commas only.
